## Align docs with the AI Gateway picker and No LLM opt-out

Context: User-facing documentation still described LLM automation as Model
Serving only, and the Ontology Wizard still told users to pick a model on that
page. The domain now saves one AI Gateway or Serving target (or No LLM) and
every in-app LLM action uses that saved target.

Changes:

1. README.md
   Mention AI Gateway or Model Serving among the Databricks services OntoBricks reuses.
2. docs/user-guide.md
   Describe the Browse picker, domain-saved target, Wizard/Auto-Map/Interpret
   behavior, and No LLM as a valid pipeline choice.
3. docs/features.md, docs/product.md, docs/INFO.md
   Replace serving-only LLM wording and document the picker plus No LLM opt-out.
4. docs/api.md, docs/data-access.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/deployment.md
   Document the combined llm-endpoints list, domain-authoritative SQL
   generation, No LLM HTTP 400, and AI Gateway FQNs on agent custom inputs.

